+    <section class="journal" aria-labelledby="journal-title">
+      <h2 id="journal-title">Roaster's Journal</h2>
+      <div class="journal-text" id="journal-text">
+        <p>Every bean we roast begins with a relationship, not a purchase order. Each year we travel to a handful of small
+          farms and cooperatives in Colombia, Ethiopia, and Guatemala, walking the rows with the people who tend them. We
+          taste the cherries at harvest, ask about their soil and shade trees, and learn how the season treated them
+          before we ever talk about price.</p>
+        <p>Back home, nothing is committed until it survives our cupping table. Samples arrive green, and we roast them
+          lightly and evenly, then slurp them blind alongside last year's favorites. We score sweetness, acidity, body,
+          and clarity, and we reject far more lots than we accept. A coffee has to taste remarkable on its own, not
+          merely good for its price.</p>
+        <p>When a lot makes the cut, we pay well above the commodity market, usually agreeing on a price before the
+          harvest so that farmers can plan their year with confidence. We buy directly or through transparent importers
+          who share their margins with us, and we publish what we paid on every bag so you can see where your money
+          goes.</p>
+        <p>Finally, we keep our purchases small and seasonal. Green coffee is shipped in modest batches, stored cool and
+          dry, and roasted weekly in our shop so it reaches your cup at its peak. When a farm's harvest runs out, we say
+          goodbye until next year and move on to the next great lot, which is why our menu changes through the seasons.
+        </p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="journal-actions">
+        <button type="button" class="btn" id="summarize-btn">Summarize</button>
+        <p class="journal-status" id="summary-status" role="status"></p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="journal-summary" id="journal-summary" hidden>
+        <h3>In short</h3>
+        <ul id="summary-list"></ul>
+      </div>
+    </section>
